For common-nine, Qwen has nine gains and zero losses, giving $p=2/2^9=.00390625$ and corrected $p=.0234375$. Olmo has eleven gains and zero losses, giving $p=.0009765625$ and corrected $p=.005859375$. Phi has one gain.

\subsection{Supplemental uncertainty and chronology}
Supplemental evaluation designs were finalized after the original model generation and before supplemental scoring. They specify the additional-input generator, solver order, alternative selectors, and analysis targets. $H_2$ uses the archived 50,000 family resamples with quantiles $1/120,119/120$ for three approximate simultaneous intervals. Its marginal intervals are $[4.17,15.00]$, $[6.67,17.50]$, and $[-2.50,2.50]$ points for Qwen, Olmo, and Phi. The primary six-comparison and supplemental three-comparison families each use their respective adjustments.

The remaining supplemental tables and curves report descriptive estimates or marginal intervals. Equal-token and fixed token-difference strata use recorded subset family IDs and saved 50,000-resample arrays. Strata with $n<12$ are reported as descriptive diagnostics. These analyses execute the saved original model outputs.
